\\workflow-format.md:370: ### Do not route on a boolean\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:393: ### Order of evaluation\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:398: 1. loop_condition of the current node    match: stay in the node, use loop_prompt\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:400: 3. global nodes                          match: enter the global node\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:414: ### `routing_prompt`\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:418: ### Self-transition\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:426: Prefer this to `loop_condition` in most cases. All routing then lives in one ordered list.\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:428: ### Loop conditions\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:430: `loop_condition` is an intent description. The routing model checks it before all transitions. When it matches, the agent stays in the node.\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:439:   \"loop_condition\": \"The user has not yet given both a full name and an email address\",\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:447: ### Tool-call transitions\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:460: Use it when the agent should decide to move, for example because of something it just said or computed. The agent can acknowledge and move in the same message. The target node's `on_enter` then asks the next question. Global nodes accept the same flag.\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:462: ### Passthrough nodes\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:486: ### Global nodes\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:526: - Use global nodes for interrupts that can happen anywhere. Do not copy the same transition into every node.\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:528: ## Extraction schema\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:611: ## End-call nodes\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:613: An `end_call` node hangs up. It has a `terminal` object and no outgoing transitions.\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:618:   \"node_type\": \"end_call\",\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:626:       \"handler\": \"__function__:end_call\",\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:658: ## Limits\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:662: | `max_node_turns` | `10` | Cap on user turns in one node. Only user messages count. Tool results and agent messages do not. There is no \"unlimited\" value |\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:672: - Give every node that sets `max_node_turns` a `max_turn_transition`. The working builder sets `max_node_turns` to 60 and 80 on its conversation nodes without a `max_turn_transition`. Its calls ended well below those counts, so the behaviour at the cap is not confirmed by it.\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:676: ## Design rules\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:680: - Every path must reach an `end_call` node.\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:686: ## Complete example\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:707:       \"max_node_turns\": 12,\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:805:       \"max_node_turns\": 20,\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:814:       \"node_type\": \"end_call\",\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:822:           \"handler\": \"__function__:end_call\",\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:829:       \"node_type\": \"end_call\",\nD:\\NR\\Build-the-Builder\\build-the-builder-v3\\build-the-builder\\docs\\workflow-format.md:837:           \"handler\": \"__function__:end_call\","}
